# Build context for the backend image is the REPOSITORY ROOT (the npm workspace
# lockfile lives there — see backend/Dockerfile). Everything below keeps the
# context small and, more importantly, keeps secrets and build noise out of the
# image.

# Dependencies are reinstalled inside the image; never ship the host's.
**/node_modules

# Build output is produced inside the image.
**/dist
**/.next
backend/dist
web/.next
web/dist

# Secrets. A container image is a poor place for a DATABASE_URL or a treasury
# key, and the backend's `.env` is the owner's local one. The image reads its
# configuration from the environment at run time, never from a baked file.
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/.env.bak-*

# Git and CI metadata are not needed to build.
.git
.gitignore
.github

# Agent scratch and skills — never part of the product.
agent
.agents
.claude
.kimi-code
.hermes
.playwright-mcp
**/.claude

# Local scratch trees the repo keeps around.
tmp-*
*.log

# Docs and the separate static docs site do not affect the image.
docs
docs-site
design
design-kit
mobile
README.md
CONTRIBUTING.md
DESIGN.md
design.tokens.json

# The web app is a separate deployable. Only its package.json is needed, so that
# `npm ci` at the workspace root resolves the lockfile without failing on the
# missing workspace — none of its source or assets belong in the backend image.
web/*
!web/package.json

# The compose file and systemd units are host-side artefacts.
docker-compose.yml
deploy

# Anything already ignored by git and obviously local.
.env
.env.*
